  "Number": 32,
  "Question": "The factors of \\(x^4+64\\) are:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\((x^2+8)^2\\)",
    "B": "\\((x^2+8)(x^2-8)\\)",
    "C": "\\((x^2+2x+4)(x^2-8x+16)\\)",
    "D": "\\((x^2-4x+8)(x^2-4x-8)\\)",
    "E": "\\((x^2-4x+8)(x^2+4x+8)\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "The square \\((x^2+8)^2\\) contains the desired terms \\(x^4\\) and \\(64\\), along with an extra \\(16x^2\\). Add and subtract that extra term to preserve the original expression:\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^4+64\n&=x^4+16x^2+64-16x^2\\\\\n&=(x^2+8)^2-(4x)^2\\\\\n&=(x^2+8-4x)(x^2+8+4x).\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nThe final step uses \\(u^2-v^2=(u-v)(u+v)\\). Thus\n\\[\nx^4+64=\\boxed{(x^2-4x+8)(x^2+4x+8)},\n\\]\nchoice E.",
